{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778941405,"nonce":"KtE0Bwx2sdaHynt57byOY2CRZzk=","title":"Graph projection: ledger relationships, deterministic layouts, live overlays","message":"## Parent\nUmbrella: 097d2b7 — Mandible canonical issue/work ledger with git-bug import/export.\n\nDepends on:\n- ff6a2bc — Ledger core.\n- e8c1d43 — operational ledger links.\n\nRelated: de2f8ac — Mandible graph workspace and provider/artifact substrate.\n\n## Scope\nMove the graph API/UI projection from ad hoc git-bug/body parsing toward canonical ledger relationships and operational overlays.\n\nThis issue owns:\n- ledger-backed issue nodes and typed issue relationship edges;\n- graph projection adapters from ledger current state/events/link tables;\n- issue mode treatment of auth requests as attached evidence/shelves by default;\n- auth/work modes where auth requests, work units, branches, commits, sessions, and artifacts can remain first-class nodes;\n- deterministic umbrella/child layouts;\n- session parent/child layout/collapse rules;\n- active/idle session actor glyph overlay contracts;\n- hidden-by-default edge labels with hover/detail/toggle access;\n- graph API display metadata for annotations, collapsed counts, relation groups, warnings, sync/conflict state, and action descriptors.\n\n## Design constraints\nThe graph is a projection, not canonical storage. Canonical relationships live in ledger/link tables. Existing provider/artifact graph tables can remain as projection/index tables where appropriate.\n\nForce layout can be used where useful, but semantic relationships should have predictable geometry:\n- umbrella parent with regularly arranged children;\n- auth evidence attached to issue nodes in issue mode;\n- dead sessions hidden from default issue graph and visible in detail history;\n- active sessions rendered as lightweight actor overlays/glyphs rather than issue-like cards.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Implementing the ledger core.\n- Replacing all graph UI in one step before ledger relationships are reliable.\n- Real-time agent animation beyond stable data/API contracts.\n\n## Verification\n- Graph API tests proving issue edges come from ledger relationships rather than body parsing.\n- Tests for auth evidence inclusion/exclusion by graph mode.\n- Tests for dead vs active/idle session representation rules.\n- Browser smoke for issue graph, work graph, activity graph, and detail pane selection.\n- Layout snapshot or structural tests for umbrella/child regularity where feasible.\n- Regression check against existing provider/artifact graph behavior.\n\n## Done means\nThe graph can use the ledger as its stable relationship source, show materially cleaner issue/auth/session structure, and avoid another backend-facing graph refactor when issue routes move fully to the ledger.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}